Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InsertReference", "ObjectName",
 CellID->283325078,ExpressionUUID->"d470f479-eb52-b333-c586-db56e91b100c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"3b903668-4db4-7c3d-f3d5-cb308340d095"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["InsertReference",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/InsertReference"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "af3349d0-9269-c5fb-08e8-42ec229eb9f0"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "adds a bibliography entry to the input notebook: a Reference cell tagged with the citation key it prompts for and labelled [key], as the citations to it read. The entry goes at the end of the bibliography rather than at the selection, and a notebook with none gets one, headed by an unnumbered References cell that prints nothing into the exported source. Where the entries come from a .bib file, that file stays the source of truth and the new entry does not reach the .tex.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["InsertReference",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/InsertReference"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "notebook", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a153342b-dfbb-0cd6-2a20-cfa3c1042f25"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "adds it to the given ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["notebook", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d65bb7ef-eb9e-bc12-d6f4-c0cf98b2a093"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["InsertReference",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/InsertReference"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"notebook", ", ", " ", "tag"}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "42434c28-17fc-bd71-84af-d50ca1708955"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "uses the given key, without prompting."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->755523467,ExpressionUUID->"ae0e225e-82cf-38e3-34c9-a937286555bc"],

Cell["\<\
Acts on the current position in the front end. There is no result to compute, \
and the function does nothing in a kernel with no front end.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c578deab-43d5-43a9-9e26-dc9290333622"],

Cell["\<\
The entry is a Reference cell tagged with the citation key and labelled with \
that key in brackets, which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so an \
entry and the citations pointing at it read alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4048eb8b-01b8-4622-ae6c-af2dfcea5d40"],

Cell["\<\
It is added at the end of the bibliography rather than at the selection, \
unlike the other block-inserting functions: a bibliography entry belongs in \
the bibliography.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"82884002-8449-4028-bb92-b6949c8f585f"],

Cell["\<\
A notebook with no bibliography yet gets one. Its heading is an unnumbered \
References cell that prints nothing into the exported source, since a \
thebibliography environment prints that heading itself and a cell emitting \
one too would put it in the compiled paper twice.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ce28af39-6e1c-4dbe-9510-43fd101546e7"],

Cell["\<\
Where the entries come from a .bib file, that file stays the source of truth: \
the entry is shown in the notebook and is not written into the exported .tex. \
A message says so.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f0964b7f-afbb-4a51-ad53-6793a845cdd9"]
}, Open  ]],

